# demo.rpn — a tour of rpn's commands. Run with:  ./rpn examples/demo.rpn
# The same file runs identically under GNU dc:  dc examples/demo.rpn

# --- arithmetic and modular exponentiation (scale 0) ---
0 k
2 3 + p c
10 4 / p c
5 3 ~ f c
2 10 ^ p c
3 v p c
10 7 % p c
2 100 1000 | p c

# --- scale factor k ---
2 k
1 3 / p c
5 3 % p c
K p c
0 k

# --- input/output bases ---
16 o 255 p c
10 o 255 p c
16 i FF p c
A i
I p O p c

# --- stack operations and printing ---
1 2 3 f c
1 2 r f c
5 d * p c
[ab] P [cd] P 10 p c
z p c
123 Z p c
1.50 Z p c
1.50 X p c

# --- strings and macros ---
[2 3 + p] x c
[[2 3 + p] x] x c
[hello] p c

# --- registers and arrays ---
42 sa la p c
5 sa [la 1 + p] sm lmx c
1 Sa 2 Sa la p La La c f
7 2 :a 2 ;a p c

# --- conditionals, loops, q/Q ---
5 sc [lc p lc 1 - sc 0 lc >m] sm lmx c
[1 p 1 Q 2 p] x 3 p c
6 sn 1 sa [la ln * sa ln 1 - sn 0 ln >m] sm lmx la p c

q